# Banking Analytics – Dataset Documentation

<p align="center">

**Enterprise Banking | Credit Risk & Portfolio Intelligence**

*Dataset Reference • Data Architecture • Analytical Coverage*

</p>

---

## 📌 1. Overview

This folder contains the synthetic banking datasets used to develop the **Enterprise Banking – Credit Risk & Portfolio Intelligence Platform** in Microsoft Power BI.

The datasets simulate a banking environment and support analysis of loan portfolios, credit risk, customer behaviour, branch performance, payment trends, and collections efficiency.

All records are fictional and created exclusively for portfolio demonstration and analytical purposes. No confidential customer, employer, or institutional data is used.

## 📂 2. Source Datasets

The project uses six core CSV datasets, organized into fact and dimension tables.

### Dimension Tables

| Dataset | Description |
|---|---|
| `Dim_Branch.csv` | Branch identifiers, names, cities, regions, managers, and annual targets |
| `Dim_Customer.csv` | Customer identifiers, demographics, age bands, income, employment type, and branch mapping |
| `Dim_Product.csv` | Loan product categories, base interest rates, and maximum tenure |

### Fact Tables

| Dataset | Description |
|---|---|
| `Fact_Loan.csv` | Loan details, disbursement amounts, outstanding balances, interest rates, loan status, and days past due |
| `Fact_Payment.csv` | Payment schedules, due amounts, paid amounts, payment channels, and payment status |
| `Fact_Collections.csv` | Collection assignments, overdue amounts, recovered amounts, resolution dates, and collection status |

## ⚙️ 3. Power BI Calculated Tables

In addition to the six source datasets, the Power BI model contains supporting tables created within Power BI using DAX.

These are model-level tables and are not separate CSV source files.

| Table | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Dim_Calendar` | Consolidated date dimension supporting date-based analysis |
| `Portfolio_Performance` | Categorizes portfolio exposure into Performing and Non-Performing |
| `Customer_Risk_Segment` | Supports customer segmentation based on NPA exposure |
| `SecurityAccess` | Maintains demonstration user access mappings for Admin, Regional, and Branch-level security |

## 📊 4. Analytical Coverage

The datasets support the following banking and credit-risk analytical areas:

- **Loan Portfolio Analysis** – Disbursed loans, outstanding balances, and portfolio composition.
- **Credit Risk & NPA Monitoring** – NPA exposure, delinquency levels, and DPD analysis.
- **Customer Analytics** – Customer demographics, income profiles, and risk segmentation.
- **Product Performance** – Loan product distribution and portfolio contribution.
- **Branch & Regional Performance** – Branch-level exposure, regional comparisons, and target achievement.
- **Collections & Recovery** – Overdue amounts, recovered amounts, and collection performance.
- **Payment Analytics** – Payment behaviour, payment status, and collection efficiency.

## 🏗️ 5. Data Model Integration

The six source datasets form the foundation of a dimensional data model implemented in Power BI.

The model includes:

- Three fact tables: `Fact_Loan`, `Fact_Payment`, and `Fact_Collections`.
- Three dimension tables: `Dim_Branch`, `Dim_Customer`, and `Dim_Product`.
- A calendar dimension for time-based reporting.
- Supporting tables for portfolio classification, customer risk segmentation, and security access.

This structure supports interactive dashboards, DAX-based calculations, cross-dimensional analysis, and dynamic Row-Level Security (RLS).

For additional details, refer to the [Data Model Documentation](../03_Data_Model/README.md).

## 🔐 6. Data Privacy & Governance

Data privacy is an important consideration throughout this portfolio project.

- All banking and customer records are synthetic.
- Customer names, identifiers, email addresses, and financial values are fictional.
- Demonstration security emails are not intended for authentication against real banking systems.
- No confidential employer, customer, or production banking data is included.
- The editable Power BI project file is maintained separately and is not included in this public repository.

## ⚠️ 7. Disclaimer

This project is an independently developed Business Intelligence portfolio demonstration.

It does not represent an actual bank, financial institution, customer portfolio, or production banking system. All datasets are fictional and intended solely for educational, analytical, and demonstration purposes.

